<title>GERMANY: OECD details German 96, 97 growth forecasts.</title>
<headline>OECD details German 96, 97 growth forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Organisation for Economic Cooperation and Development published the following economic forecasts for Germany in its Economic Survey of Germany. The main forecasts are unchanged from the previously published report on world economic growth:</p>
<p>				   1995	   1996	   1997</p>
<p> Real GDP			 1.9	    0.5	    2.4</p>
<p>				 H1    H2     H1    H2     H1    H2</p>
<p>				2.0   0.8   -0.3   1.9    2.5   2.6</p>
<p> GDP deflator		   2.2	    1.5	    1.3</p>
<p> Unemployment pct	     9.4	   10.3	   10.4</p>
<p> Total fixed investment     1.5	   -2.4	    2.5</p>
<p>    construction		1.2	   -3.8	    1.4</p>
<p>    machinery &amp; equipment   2.0	   unch	    4.2</p>
<p> Stockbuilding		 unch	   -0.5	    0.1</p>
<p> Private consumption	  1.7	    1.3	    2.0</p>
<p> Private cons. deflator     2.0	    1.6	    1.5</p>
<p> Govt consumption	     2.1	    1.4	    1.4</p>
<p> Total domestic demand	1.7	   unch	    2.1</p>
<p> Net exports		    0.3	    0.5	    0.3</p>
<p>     exports goods+svcs     3.8	    5.3	    6.9</p>
<p>     imports goods+svcs     2.7	    3.2	    5.9</p>
<p> Govt budget def (pct GDP) -3.5	   -4.0	   -3.4</p>
<p>-- Ashley Seager, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
</text>
